.TH NOXFORGE-OPACITY 1 "September 2026" "NoxForge 13.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
noxforge-opacity \- configure transparency and depth for NoxForge Plasma themes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B noxforge-opacity
.RB [ \-\-gui ]
.RB [ \-\-preset
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-\-level
.IR 10\-100 ]
.RB [ \-\-status ]
.RB [ \-\-reset ]
.RB [ \-\-dry-run ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-aurorae ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B noxforge-opacity
allows users to inspect, customize, and reset transparency levels across
NoxForge Plasma Desktop Themes and Aurorae window decorations on KDE Plasma 6.
It modifies translucent SVG assets in the user's local directory, invalidates
Plasma caches, and signals the desktop shell to update dynamically.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-gui
Launch the Qt 6 graphical configurator with real-time desktop preview.
.TP
.BI \-\-preset " name"
Apply a predefined transparency recipe: solid, original, frost, glass, ultra.
.TP
.BI \-\-level " percent"
Apply a uniform opacity percentage (10 to 100).
.TP
.B \-\-status
Show current opacity levels of installed themes.
.TP
.B \-\-reset
Restore original upstream NoxForge opacity values.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Simulate modifications without writing to disk or restarting services.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON output.
.TP
.B \-\-aurorae
Apply transparency adjustments to Aurorae window decoration frames.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 1 on error, and 2 for invalid command arguments.
.SH AUTHOR
NoxForge Contributors.
